{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99390","id":2185066746,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6CPXj6","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99390","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99390.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99390.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99390","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99390/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99390/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99390/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/31fc58f11ab119c744f5272d32c4858f8284b1fd","number":99390,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make Camera2D smoothing more framerate independent","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Currently Camera2D smoothing uses lerp smoothing multiplied by delta, this is an approximation that's not entirely framerate independent but is, probably, usually fine in most cases. However it's still not perfect and this aims to fix that, implementing the algorithm shown here https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LSNQuFEDOyQ.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0c0b057-0edb-49b7-b41b-ee346565b436\r\n\r\n\r\nMain issue I could find with the current implementation is, if under circumstances that allow it, delta happens to be more than 1 second, smoothing will break and overshoot it's destination.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/691aeaa0-f463-483a-a65f-6381d0756a7a\r\n\r\nThis fixes that.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da9a6f27-f3fb-4199-a61d-5ee86100f34f\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- I applied this to both rotation and position smoothing.\r\n- The general speed seems to be roughly the exact same so I don't believe this breaks compat.\r\n- This is obviously slightly more expensive (didn't test by how much), so I imagine whether this PR lands or not will depend on if it's deemed worth it, especially since by default `delta` is capped at ~0.125.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4